  "question": {
    "text": "A man on the top of a vertical tower observes a car moving at a uniform speed towards the tower on a horizontal road. If it takes&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>18</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>min</mi></math>&nbsp;for the angle of depression of the car to change from <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>30</mn><mo>&#176;</mo></math>&nbsp;to&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>45</mn><mo>&#176;</mo></math>,&nbsp;then the time taken (in <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>min</mi></math>)&nbsp;by the car to reach the foot of the tower is",
